From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tile-view <tile-view@localhost>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:47:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] Mobile: Let the tile view notebook picker select
 individually from All notebooks, and show subnotebook hierarchy clearly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Previously an empty selection meant "all" and every checkbox showed
unchecked, so there was no way to deselect a single notebook while
starting from "all". The dialog now works on an explicit working set of
selected notebook IDs: opening it with the stored "all" value seeds the
set with every visible notebook, the "All notebooks" row is checked
exactly when all of them are selected, and confirming stores an empty
value again when everything is still selected (keeping new notebooks
included automatically) or the explicit ID list otherwise. The set is
only written to the setting when the user presses Done -- the confirm
button is disabled while nothing is selected, and shows how many
notebooks are currently selected.

Also increase the per-level indent, add a "└" marker for nested rows, and
since the checkbox component has no indeterminate state, show a parent
notebook as unchecked with a "(n/m)" count when only some of its
descendants are selected -- the underlying tree-building logic was
already correctly nesting notebooks by parent_id, so the flat appearance
on device came down to the 20px indent being too subtle and the
unfiltered trash/notebook list adding noise, both addressed by this and
the previous commit.

